{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"55063","self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/55063","key":"SV-8929","renderedFields":{"statuscategorychangedate":"Today 9:05 AM","issuetype":null,"timespent":null,"project":null,"customfield_10351":"","fixVersions":null,"aggregatetimespent":null,"statusCategory":null,"resolution":null,"resolutiondate":null,"workratio":null,"watches":null,"issuerestriction":null,"lastViewed":null,"created":"Today 9:05 AM","customfield_10021":null,"customfield_10385":null,"priority":null,"labels":null,"customfield_10016":null,"customfield_10019":null,"timeestimate":null,"aggregatetimeoriginalestimate":null,"versions":null,"customfield_10418":null,"customfield_10419":null,"issuelinks":null,"assignee":null,"updated":"Today 9:05 AM","status":null,"components":null,"timeoriginalestimate":null,"description":"<h3><a name=\"1.Whathappensnow\"></a>1. What happens now</h3>\n\n<p>The Inventory Value report remembers the category and vendor a user picked. If one of those saved choices later stops existing in the data, the report keeps using it anyway. The result is a report that opens showing nothing, with no explanation, and no obvious way for the user to work out why - the filter that is emptying the report is one they cannot see any more.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"2.Whatshouldhappeninstead\"></a>2. What should happen instead</h3>\n\n<p>Inventory Value requirement S8-R6: \"Restore is defensive: a saved value that is no longer valid falls back to that setting's default rather than breaking the view. A saved category or vendor no longer present in the data is dropped.\"</p>\n\n<p>So the stale choice should be quietly discarded on load and the report should open on its normal full list.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"3.Howtoseeit\"></a>3. How to see it</h3>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Sign in and open <b>Reports</b> &gt; <b>Inventory Value</b>.</li>\n\t<li>Choose a category in the <b>Category</b> filter, so the choice is saved.</li>\n\t<li>Make that saved choice no longer valid - the quickest reliable way is to change the stored category to one that does not exist in the data.</li>\n\t<li>Reload the report.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<p><b>Exact test data this was seen with:</b> the saved category was replaced with the identifier <tt>00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000</tt>, which matches no category in this organisation. Locations <b>Staging Heavy Duty - 9919</b> and <b>Staging Lethbridge - 4310</b>, date range <b>This Month</b>, 5,657 rows in scope before the change.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"4.Whatwasactuallyseen\"></a>4. What was actually seen</h3>\n\n<p>The report loaded without an error message, but:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>the stale category was <b>not</b> dropped - it was still there in the saved settings afterwards, unchanged;</li>\n\t<li>it was still being applied, so the table came back with <b>no data rows at all</b>, down from 5,657.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p>The user is left looking at an empty report caused by a filter selection that no longer corresponds to anything.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"5.Whatwasruledout\"></a>5. What was ruled out</h3>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><b>It is not a crash.</b> The page renders and no error is shown - which is part of the problem, because nothing tells the user what happened.</li>\n\t<li><b>It is not the rest of the restoring.</b> The date range, locations, columns and sort were all restored correctly in the same load, so the restore path itself is running.</li>\n\t<li><b>It is not a stale-cache effect.</b> The saved settings were re-read after the load and the invalid identifier was still present.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<h3><a name=\"6.Howoften\"></a>6. How often</h3>\n\n<p>Every time.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"7.Whereitwasseen\"></a>7. Where it was seen</h3>\n\n<p>Reports &gt; Inventory Value, on the QA branch, build v3.5-16cf83f, on 6 August 2026.</p>","customfield_10015":null,"timetracking":{},"security":null,"aggregatetimeestimate":null,"attachment":[],"summary":null,"creator":null,"subtasks":null,"customfield_10285":"","reporter":null,"customfield_10044":null,"aggregateprogress":null,"customfield_10046":null,"customfield_10047":null,"environment":"","customfield_10318":null,"duedate":null,"customfield_10518":null,"progress":null,"votes":null,"comment":{"comments":[],"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/55063/comment","maxResults":0,"total":0,"startAt":0},"worklog":{"startAt":0,"maxResults":20,"total":0,"worklogs":[]}},"fields":{"statuscategorychangedate":"2026-08-05T23:05:50.030-0500","issuetype":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issuetype/10007","id":"10007","description":"Subtasks track small pieces of work that are part of a larger task. (Migrated on 31 Dec 2023 09:01 UTC)","iconUrl":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10854?size=medium","name":"Story Defect","subtask":true,"avatarId":10854,"entityId":"0900502c-ae66-465f-a9da-8322307b07ff","hierarchyLevel":-1},"parent":{"id":"54696","key":"SV-8675","self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/54696","fields":{"summary":"Inv Value - Story 8 - Column Selection and Persistence","status":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/status/10349","description":"","iconUrl":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/","name":"Open","id":"10349","statusCategory":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/statuscategory/2","id":2,"key":"new","colorName":"blue-gray","name":"To Do"}},"priority":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/priority/3","iconUrl":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/images/icons/priorities/medium_new.svg","name":"Medium","id":"3"},"issuetype":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issuetype/10245","id":"10245","description":"Stories track functionality or features expressed as user goals.","iconUrl":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10315?size=medium","name":"Story","subtask":false,"avata